  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal for a change of use from a residential dwelling (Use Class C3), to a children's home (C2) would be contrary to Policy 6 (i) of the Havering Local Plan as there is no identified need within the borough for additional places. As there is no identified need, the proposal results in the unacceptable loss of a residential dwelling, which is contrary to Policy 3 (xi) of the Havering Local Plan.",
    "The proposed development due to its inadequate on-site car parking provision would likely result in unacceptable overspill onto surrounding roads, causing harm to highway safety and residential amenity, and contrary to Policies to Havering Local Plan Policies 6 (ix) (x), 23 and 24, London Plan Policies T4, T6 and the NPPF (2021).",
    "Statement Required by Article 35 (2) of the Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015: Consideration was given to seeking amendments, but given conflict with adopted planning policy, notification of intended refusal and the reason(s) for it was given to Mr Taheem (Agent) by e-mail on 12/09/25."
